Sylvia Isler wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> I would like to foward some mail from my current account which is
> on a VMS machine to  another machine. Can someone tell me how
> this is done?  I know that in unix it is very simple (just create
> a .forward file). I'm hoping with VMS it is equally as simple.
> 
> Thanks in advance,
> 
> Sylvia

In principle it is simple. In MAIL use

MAIL> SET FORWARD <remote-user>

To see what you've set use

MAIL> SHOW FORWARD

Of course what you put in the <remote-user> field depends on the
transport you are using between the local and remote system. If
DECnet, it would be of the form
REMOTE::USER
or if using SMTP mail, something like
"SMTP%""user@remote.node"""
Note the number of "! What goes in front of the % depends on the details
of the local system - I use the MX mailer on our VMS systems, so I'd
have
"MX%""user@remote.node"""

I'm sure there are some possibilities I've omitted.

Hope this helps.
Regards,
John Hill

